arXiv:2609.03224v1 Announce Type: new 
Abstract: In this paper, we consider one-dimensional discrete Schr\"odinger operators \begin{align}
  Hu(n)=(\Delta+V)u(n)\nonumber \end{align}
  on $\ell^2(\mathbb{N})$ with a self-adjoint boundary condition at $n=0$, where $\Delta$ denotes the discrete Laplacian and $V(n)$ is a real-valued perturbation satisfying
  $$V(n)=\frac{O(1)}{1+n}.$$ We determine the sharp transition for the asymptotic coefficient of \(V\) governing the existence and nonexistence of embedded eigenvalues.
